/*!
@defgroup flexcan
@ingroup mod_communication Controller Area Network with Flexible Data Rate (FlexCAN)
@brief Hardware CAN / CAN-FD communication controller for the YTMicro SDK.

@details
The FlexCAN module implements a full CAN 2.0 B and CAN FD protocol engine.
It provides hardware-based message filtering, flexible message buffers (MBs),
an optional receive FIFO, and DMA-assisted transfer capability.

@section flexcan_features Key Features
- Full CAN 2.0 B and CAN FD protocol engine (ISO 11898-1 compliant).
- Configurable message buffers — each independently set as Tx or Rx
  (see @ref FEATURE_CAN_MAX_MB_NUM for the per-device maximum).
- Standard (11-bit) and extended (29-bit) identifiers.
- CAN FD payloads up to 64 bytes with bit-rate switching (BRS)
  (see @ref FEATURE_CAN_HAS_FD for per-platform availability).
- 6-message-deep Rx FIFO with up to 128/256/512 acceptance filters.
- Enhanced Rx FIFO on supported devices
  (see @ref FEATURE_CAN_HAS_ENHANCE_RX_FIFO).
- DMA-assisted Rx FIFO readout on supported devices
  (see @ref FEATURE_CAN_HAS_DMA_ENABLE).
- Individual Rx mask register per message buffer.
- Transmission abort capability.
- Programmable bit timing and prescaler.
- Selectable PE clock source (oscillator or peripheral clock)
  (see @ref FEATURE_CAN_HAS_PE_CLKSRC_SELECT).
- Pretended Networking wake-up in Stop mode
  (see @ref FEATURE_CAN_HAS_PRETENDED_NETWORKING).
- Self Wake-Up from Stop mode
  (see @ref FEATURE_CAN_HAS_SELF_WAKE_UP).
- Transceiver Delay Compensation (TDC) for CAN FD at higher data rates.
- RAM ECC error detection and correction on supported devices
  (see @ref FEATURE_CAN_HAS_RAM_ECC).
- Listen-Only and Loop-Back diagnostic modes.

@section flexcan_modes Supported Operation Modes

| Mode                   | Enum Value              | Description                                                  |
|------------------------|-------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------|
| Normal                 | FLEXCAN_NORMAL_MODE     | Standard transmit/receive operation.                         |
| Listen-Only            | FLEXCAN_LISTEN_ONLY_MODE| Bus monitoring without acknowledgement or transmission.      |
| Loopback               | FLEXCAN_LOOPBACK_MODE   | Internal loop-back for self-test (self reception enabled).   |
| Freeze                 | FLEXCAN_FREEZE_MODE     | Module halted; registers accessible for configuration.       |
| Disable                | FLEXCAN_DISABLE_MODE    | Module clock gated, lowest power consumption.                |

@section flexcan_arch Module Architecture

@verbatim
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                  Application Code                    │
│            (calls FLEXCAN_DRV_* functions)           │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│        FlexCAN Driver Layer (flexcan_driver.h/c)     │
│  ● Instance-based API (FLEXCAN_DRV_Init, etc.)       │
│  ● Uses instance index (0..N) to resolve base addr   │
│  ● IRQ dispatch (flexcan_irq.h/c)                    │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│   FlexCAN HW Access Layer (flexcan_hw_access.h/c)    │
│  ● Direct register-level access (inline + non-inline)│
│  ● Mostly inline functions for performance           │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│            FlexCAN Peripheral Hardware               │
│      (MCR, CTRL1/2, ESR1, MB RAM, RXIMR, etc.)       │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
@endverbatim

@subsection flexcan_arch_driver Driver Layer (flexcan_driver.h)
Application code should **only** use the `FLEXCAN_DRV_*` functions from
flexcan_driver.h. These functions accept a zero-based **instance** index
and resolve the hardware base address internally.

@subsection flexcan_arch_hw HW Access Layer (flexcan_hw_access.h)
This internal layer provides low-level register accessors organized into
functional groups:
- **Module Enable & Mode Control** — FLEXCAN_Enable(), FLEXCAN_Disable(),
  FLEXCAN_EnterFreezeMode(), FLEXCAN_ExitFreezeMode(), etc.
- **Clock & Bit Timing** — FLEXCAN_SetTimeSegments(), FLEXCAN_GetTimeSegments(), etc.
- **FD Configuration** — FLEXCAN_SetFDEnabled(), FLEXCAN_SetPayloadSize(), etc.
- **Message Buffer Operations** — FLEXCAN_SetTxMsgBuff(), FLEXCAN_SetRxMsgBuff(), etc.
- **Rx FIFO** — FLEXCAN_EnableRxFifo(), FLEXCAN_ReadRxFifo(), etc.
- **Enhanced Rx FIFO** — FLEXCAN_EnableEnhanceRxFifo(), FLEXCAN_ReadEnhanceRxFifo(), etc.
- **Interrupt & Status** — FLEXCAN_SetMsgBuffIntCmd(), FLEXCAN_SetErrIntCmd(), etc.
- **Pretended Networking** — FLEXCAN_ConfigPN(), FLEXCAN_SetPN(), etc.

@section flexcan_config Configuration Parameters

@subsection flexcan_config_struct flexcan_user_config_t Fields
| Field                              | Type                                 | Description                                                      |
|------------------------------------|--------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------|
| max_num_mb                         | uint32_t                             | Maximum number of message buffers to use.                        |
| num_id_filters                     | flexcan_rx_fifo_id_filter_num_t      | Number of Rx FIFO ID filters (when FIFO enabled).                |
| is_rx_fifo_needed                  | bool                                 | Enable/disable the Rx FIFO feature.                              |
| flexcanMode                        | flexcan_operation_modes_t            | Operation mode (Normal, Listen-Only, Loopback, Freeze, Disable). |
| payload                            | flexcan_fd_payload_size_t            | Payload size (8 / 16 / 32 / 64 bytes; FD only for >8).          |
| fd_enable                          | bool                                 | Enable/disable CAN FD support.                                   |
| pe_clock                           | flexcan_clk_source_t                 | Protocol Engine clock source (oscillator or peripheral).         |
| bitrate                            | flexcan_time_segment_t               | Bit timing for standard / arbitration phase.                     |
| bitrate_cbt                        | flexcan_time_segment_t               | Bit timing for FD data phase.                                    |
| transfer_type                      | flexcan_rx_fifo_transfer_type_t      | Rx FIFO transfer method (interrupt or DMA).                      |
| rxFifoDMAChannel                   | uint8_t                              | DMA channel number for Rx FIFO DMA transfers.                    |

@subsection flexcan_config_features Device Feature Macros
| Macro                                  | Description                                                |
|----------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------|
| FEATURE_CAN_HAS_FD                     | Set to 1 if device supports CAN FD.                       |
| FEATURE_CAN_HAS_PE_CLKSRC_SELECT      | Set to 1 if PE clock source is selectable.                 |
| FEATURE_CAN_HAS_DMA_ENABLE            | Set to 1 if DMA is available for Rx FIFO.                  |
| FEATURE_CAN_HAS_ENHANCE_RX_FIFO       | Set to 1 if Enhanced Rx FIFO is available.                 |
| FEATURE_CAN_HAS_PRETENDED_NETWORKING   | Set to 1 if Pretended Networking is available.             |
| FEATURE_CAN_HAS_SELF_WAKE_UP          | Set to 1 if Self Wake-Up feature is available.             |
| FEATURE_CAN_HAS_RAM_ECC               | Set to 1 if RAM ECC detection/correction is available.     |
| FEATURE_CAN_MAX_MB_NUM                 | Maximum number of message buffers on the device.           |

@section flexcan_usage Usage Patterns

@subsection flexcan_usage_basic Pattern 1: Basic Initialization and Send

@code{.c}
#define INST_CANCOM1 (0U)
#define TX_MAILBOX   (1U)
#define MSG_ID       (0x100U)

flexcan_state_t canState;
flexcan_user_config_t canConfig;

// Step 1: Get default configuration (500 Kbit/s, 16 MBs, no FD, no FIFO)
FLEXCAN_DRV_GetDefaultConfig(&canConfig);

// Step 2: Initialize FlexCAN instance
FLEXCAN_DRV_Init(INST_CANCOM1, &canState, &canConfig);

// Step 3: Configure a Tx mailbox
flexcan_data_info_t txInfo = {
    .data_length = 8U,
    .msg_id_type = FLEXCAN_MSG_ID_STD,
    .is_remote   = false
};
FLEXCAN_DRV_ConfigTxMb(INST_CANCOM1, TX_MAILBOX, &txInfo, MSG_ID);

// Step 4: Send data (blocking, 1000 ms timeout)
uint8_t txData[8] = { 0x01, 0x02, 0x03, 0x04, 0x05, 0x06, 0x07, 0x08 };
FLEXCAN_DRV_SendBlocking(INST_CANCOM1, TX_MAILBOX, &txInfo, MSG_ID, txData, 1000U);

// Step 5: De-initialize when done
FLEXCAN_DRV_Deinit(INST_CANCOM1);
@endcode

@subsection flexcan_usage_receive Pattern 2: Basic Receive (Non-Blocking)

@code{.c}
#define INST_CANCOM1 (0U)
#define RX_MAILBOX   (2U)
#define MSG_ID       (0x200U)

flexcan_data_info_t rxInfo = {
    .data_length = 8U,
    .msg_id_type = FLEXCAN_MSG_ID_STD
};

// Configure Rx mailbox
FLEXCAN_DRV_ConfigRxMb(INST_CANCOM1, RX_MAILBOX, &rxInfo, MSG_ID);

// Start non-blocking receive
flexcan_msgbuff_t recvBuff;
FLEXCAN_DRV_Receive(INST_CANCOM1, RX_MAILBOX, &recvBuff);

// Poll transfer status
while (FLEXCAN_DRV_GetTransferStatus(INST_CANCOM1, RX_MAILBOX) == STATUS_BUSY);
@endcode

@subsection flexcan_usage_rxfifo Pattern 3: Rx FIFO Reception

@code{.c}
#define INST_CANCOM1 (0U)

// ID Filter table (Format A)
const flexcan_id_table_t filterTable[] = {
    { .isExtendedFrame = false, .isRemoteFrame = false, .id = 1U },
    { .isExtendedFrame = false, .isRemoteFrame = false, .id = 2U }
};

// Configure Rx FIFO filters
FLEXCAN_DRV_ConfigRxFifo(INST_CANCOM1, FLEXCAN_RX_FIFO_ID_FORMAT_A, filterTable);

// Blocking FIFO reception (1000 ms timeout)
flexcan_msgbuff_t fifoBuff;
status_t status = FLEXCAN_DRV_RxFifoBlocking(INST_CANCOM1, &fifoBuff, 1000U);
@endcode

@subsection flexcan_usage_callback Pattern 4: Callback-based Operation

@code{.c}
void myFlexcanCallback(uint8_t instance, flexcan_event_type_t eventType,
                       uint32_t buffIdx, flexcan_state_t *state)
{
    if (eventType == FLEXCAN_EVENT_TX_COMPLETE) {
        // Transmission complete
    }
    if (eventType == FLEXCAN_EVENT_RX_COMPLETE) {
        // Reception complete — data in state->mbs[buffIdx].mb_message
    }
}

// Install event callback
FLEXCAN_DRV_InstallEventCallback(INST_CANCOM1, myFlexcanCallback, NULL);

// Install error callback
void myErrorCallback(uint8_t instance, flexcan_error_event_type_t errorType,
                     flexcan_state_t *state)
{
    // Handle error events
}
FLEXCAN_DRV_InstallErrorCallback(INST_CANCOM1, myErrorCallback, NULL);
@endcode

@section flexcan_api API Quick Reference

@subsection flexcan_api_init Initialization & De-initialization
| Function                        | Description                                           |
|---------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------|
| FLEXCAN_DRV_GetDefaultConfig()  | Fill configuration struct with device defaults.       |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_Init()              | Initialize FlexCAN instance with user configuration.  |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_Deinit()            | Shut down FlexCAN instance, disable interrupts.       |

@subsection flexcan_api_bitrate Bit Rate Configuration
| Function                        | Description                                           |
|---------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------|
| FLEXCAN_DRV_SetBitrate()        | Set standard / arbitration phase bit timing.          |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_SetBitrateCbt()     | Set CAN FD data phase bit timing.                     |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_GetBitrate()        | Get current standard / arbitration phase bit timing.  |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_GetBitrateFD()      | Get current CAN FD data phase bit timing.             |

@subsection flexcan_api_mask Rx Mask Configuration
| Function                              | Description                                       |
|---------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|
| FLEXCAN_DRV_SetRxMaskType()           | Set Rx mask mode (global or individual).          |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_SetRxFifoGlobalMask()     | Set Rx FIFO global acceptance mask.               |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_SetRxMbGlobalMask()       | Set Rx MB global acceptance mask (std/ext).       |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_SetRxMb14Mask()           | Set Rx MB 14 acceptance mask.                     |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_SetRxMb15Mask()           | Set Rx MB 15 acceptance mask.                     |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_SetRxIndividualMask()     | Set individual acceptance mask for a specific MB. |

@subsection flexcan_api_tx Transmit Operations
| Function                              | Description                                       |
|---------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|
| FLEXCAN_DRV_ConfigTxMb()              | Configure a message buffer for transmission.      |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_ConfigRemoteResponseMb()  | Configure a Tx MB for remote frame response.      |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_SendBlocking()            | Send a CAN frame (blocking with timeout).         |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_Send()                    | Send a CAN frame (non-blocking, callback-based).  |

@subsection flexcan_api_rx Receive Operations
| Function                              | Description                                       |
|---------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|
| FLEXCAN_DRV_ConfigRxMb()              | Configure a message buffer for reception.         |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_ConfigRxFifo()            | Configure Rx FIFO ID filter table.                |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_ConfigEnhanceRxFifo()     | Configure Enhanced Rx FIFO filter table.          |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_ReceiveBlocking()         | Receive via MB (blocking with timeout).           |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_Receive()                 | Receive via MB (non-blocking, callback-based).    |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_RxFifoBlocking()          | Receive via Rx FIFO (blocking with timeout).      |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_RxFifo()                  | Receive via Rx FIFO (non-blocking).               |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_EnhanceRxFifo()           | Receive via Enhanced Rx FIFO (non-blocking).      |

@subsection flexcan_api_status Transfer Status & Error
| Function                              | Description                                       |
|---------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|
| FLEXCAN_DRV_AbortTransfer()           | Abort an ongoing transfer on a specific MB.       |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_GetTransferStatus()       | Get the current transfer status of a MB.          |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_GetErrorStatus()          | Read the ESR1 error/status register.              |

@subsection flexcan_api_callback Callback & Interrupt
| Function                              | Description                                       |
|---------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|
| FLEXCAN_DRV_InstallEventCallback()    | Register a callback for Tx/Rx/FIFO events.        |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_InstallErrorCallback()    | Register a callback for error events.             |

@subsection flexcan_api_tdc Transceiver Delay Compensation
| Function                              | Description                                       |
|---------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|
| FLEXCAN_DRV_SetTDCOffset()            | Enable/disable TDC and set offset value.          |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_GetTDCValue()             | Read the measured TDC value.                      |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_GetTDCFail()              | Check if TDC measurement failed.                  |
| FLEXCAN_DRV_ClearTDCFail()            | Clear the TDC fail flag.                          |

@subsection flexcan_api_pn Pretended Networking
| Function                              | Description                                       |
|---------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|
| FLEXCAN_DRV_ConfigPN()                | Configure and enable/disable Pretended Networking.|
| FLEXCAN_DRV_GetWMB()                  | Read a wake-up message buffer after PN wake.      |

@section flexcan_notes Important Notes

@subsection flexcan_notes_clock Clock Dependency
The FlexCAN peripheral clock must be configured via the @ref clock_manager
**before** calling FLEXCAN_DRV_Init(). The driver does not manage clocks
internally. Pin multiplexing must also be configured externally.

@subsection flexcan_notes_fifo Rx FIFO Constraints
- When Rx FIFO is enabled, MB 0 is reserved for FIFO output and cannot be
  used for individual transmission.
- The number of MBs consumed by the FIFO depends on the number of ID filters
  configured.
- DMA module must be initialized **prior to** FlexCAN Rx FIFO usage in DMA
  mode; the DMA channel must be allocated by the application.

@subsection flexcan_notes_blocking Blocking API Behavior
- When FLEXCAN_DRV_ReceiveBlocking() or FLEXCAN_DRV_SendBlocking() is called
  with timeout = 0 and the message is already in the mailbox, the function
  reports timeout but the message may still have been transmitted/received.
- Do **not** call blocking receive (FLEXCAN_DRV_ReceiveBlocking /
  FLEXCAN_DRV_RxFifoBlocking) or FLEXCAN_DRV_AbortTransfer inside a callback
  without first polling the previous operation status. This leads to
  undefined behavior.

@subsection flexcan_notes_alignment Memory Alignment
For Cortex-M0 devices (YTM32B1LD0, YTM32B1LE0), transmission and reception
buffers must be memory-aligned. The only exceptions are FLEXCAN_DRV_Send(),
FLEXCAN_DRV_SendBlocking(), and FLEXCAN_DRV_ConfigRemoteResponseMb() with a
payload length less than 3 bytes.

@subsection flexcan_notes_pn Pretended Networking
When using Pretended Networking in Stop mode, the CHI (interface) clock must
be disabled and the PE clock source must remain enabled as configured in the
CAN module. Ensure the CHI clock is re-enabled on wake-up to Run mode.

@section flexcan_integration Integration Guide

@subsection flexcan_integration_files Compilation Units
The following source files must be added to the project build:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/flexcan/flexcan_driver.c
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/flexcan/flexcan_hw_access.c
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/flexcan/flexcan_irq.c
@endverbatim

@subsection flexcan_integration_include Include Paths
Add the following directory to the toolchain include path:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/inc/
@endverbatim

@subsection flexcan_integration_symbols Compile Symbols
No special compile-time symbols are required for this module. Device-specific
feature macros (`FEATURE_CAN_*`) are automatically defined in the device
features header.

@subsection flexcan_integration_deps Dependencies
- @ref clock_manager — Required for enabling the FlexCAN peripheral clock.
- @ref interrupt_manager — Required for FlexCAN interrupt installation.
- @ref dma_driver — Required when using Rx FIFO in DMA transfer mode.

*/
